# Local development configuration.
#
# Copy to .env.local and fill in what you need. Every value is OPTIONAL:
# an unset variable means that feature is simply off, and the site still runs.
#
# Everything here is PUBLIC: Vite inlines VITE_* values into the bundle that
# ships to every visitor. Never put a credential in this file.
#
# In CI these are set as GitHub Actions *variables* on the dev and prod
# Environments, not as secrets. See .github/workflows/deploy.yaml.

# Canonical origin. Used for canonical links, og:url, and the robots.txt,
# sitemap.xml and llms.txt the build writes into dist/ (none without it).
# Leave unset locally: the runtime origin is used instead.
# VITE_SITE_URL=https://example.com

# Contact-form endpoint (the Lambda Function URL from the contact add-on).
# Unset: the form runs as a labelled demo that discards every message
# (VITE_CONTACT_MODE, "mock" by default; "off" replaces it with a
# "call or email us" notice).
# VITE_CONTACT_ENDPOINT=https://xxxxx.lambda-url.eu-north-1.on.aws/

# Consent-record endpoint (the consent add-on).
# Unset: consent decisions stay in the visitor's browser only.
# VITE_CONSENT_ENDPOINT=https://xxxxx.lambda-url.eu-north-1.on.aws/

# Visit statistics (doc/visit-tracking.md). Unset: every page view of a
# production build goes to HA Group's CRM, ANALYTICS_ENDPOINT in
# src/config/site.ts. "off" sends nothing. A development server, localhost and
# `make preview` never send anything, whatever this says.
# VITE_ANALYTICS_ENDPOINT=off
